1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,540
 This is how I turn my feet into walking trampolines.

2
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:10,260
 First, I do isometric holds at the start of my workout.

3
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:14,260
 This helped push my vertical over 40 inches, but out of all the training I've ever done,

4
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:16,580
 these are the simplest and most effective exercises.

5
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:18,180
 It only takes 3 minutes.

6
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:20,820
 First, get into a split position with your heel elevated.

7
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:22,140
 Hold this for 30 seconds.

8
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:25,580
 Studies have shown this little heel elevation to be more effective for ankle stiffness and

9
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:26,580
 stability in the knee.

10
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:28,760
 I do 3 sets of 30 seconds each side.

11
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:31,320
 The next movement is almost the exact same thing.

12
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:35,080
 We're still keeping the heel elevated, but now while doing short hops because it's important

13
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:37,040
 to feel that elasticity in your tendons.

14
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:38,880
 Do this for 3 sets of 12 each side.

15
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:42,360
 And since the only goal is stiffer ankles, you can do this anywhere using just about

16
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:43,520
 anything you have available.

17
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:47,160
 Make sure you're still doing strength movements to support your joints, strength, and general

18
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:48,160
 athleticism.

19
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:51,080
 That's the real secret to eye-catching hops in spring-loaded feet.

20
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:52,520
 This is how I turn my feet into walking trampolines.

